# Architecture

## What This Is
A multi-tenant company operating system for SPLYTS. Stores company knowledge, manages work, and generates outputs — replacing scattered docs, drives, and tools.

## Stack
- **Frontend + API:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Database + Auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL, RLS enforced)
- **AI:** Anthropic Claude via API routes only — never called from client
- **Deploy:** Vercel
- **Language:** TypeScript strict throughout

## Folder Structure
```
app/
  (auth)/login/          ← auth pages
  (dashboard)/           ← all authenticated pages
    layout.tsx           ← sidebar shell
    page.tsx             ← dashboard home
api/                     ← all API routes (AI calls live here)
lib/
  supabase/
    client.ts            ← browser client
    server.ts            ← server client for API routes
  ai/
    prompts.ts           ← ALL prompts live here, nowhere else
    generate.ts          ← AI call logic
  types/
    database.ts          ← generated from Supabase schema
components/              ← shared UI components
supabase/migrations/     ← schema as code, never touch DB directly
```

## Multi-Tenant Rule
Every org's data is isolated by `organization_id`. See `database.mdc` for query rules.

## Reusability
This codebase is a generic company OS platform. It contains zero company-specific code. Company identity (name, brand, voice) lives in the database as data rows, never as hardcoded strings. Copying this repo and pointing it at a new Supabase project creates a fully functional OS for a new company with zero code changes. See `template-ready.mdc` for the hard rules.

## Repo Independence
This is a standalone company OS. It does not know about, depend on, or reference any other repo. A separate `hub-os` repo may connect to this system's database as a read-only consumer — but this repo has no knowledge of that connection. See `repo-boundary.mdc` and `independence-test.mdc` for enforcement.
